      "id": "vmp",
      "chapter": 19,
      "name": "Value of Marginal Product and Labor Demand",
      "definition": "VMP = P x MPL. The dollar value of the additional output from one more worker.",
      "key_insight": "A profit-maximizing firm hires workers until VMP = Wage. The VMP curve IS the labor demand curve. If the output price rises, VMP shifts up, demand for labor increases, wages rise.",
