      "name": "Consumer Choice: Budget Constraints and Indifference Curves",
      "definition": "Consumers maximize utility subject to their budget constraint. Optimal choice: MRS = Px/Py.",
      "key_insight": "The budget constraint shows what you CAN buy. Indifference curves show what you WANT. The optimal point is where the highest indifference curve just touches the budget line (tangency). At tangency, the rate you're WILLING to trade X for Y (MRS) equals the rate the MARKET lets you trade (Px/Py).",
      "depends_on": [],
      "leads_to": [
        "income_substitution_effects"
      ],
      "equations": [
