      "id": "political_economy",
      "chapter": 23,
      "name": "Political Economy: Voting and Arrow's Theorem",
      "definition": "Condorcet Paradox: majority voting can produce cyclical (intransitive) preferences. Arrow's Impossibility Theorem: no voting system can satisfy all desirable properties simultaneously.",
      "key_insight": "In pairwise voting, compare every pair of options. Check who wins each matchup based on voter counts. If A beats B, B beats C, but C beats A -- that's the Condorcet Paradox (cyclical).",
