      "vision_extract": "## STRUCTURED ANALYSIS - SLIDE 97\n\n### 1) MAIN CONCEPT/TOPIC\n**Government Budget Deficits and Surpluses in the Loanable Funds Framework**\n- Active learning exercise analyzing how changes in government fiscal position affect financial markets\n- Focus on transition from balanced budget to deficit scenarios and surplus analysis\n\n### 2) EQUATIONS SHOWN\n**None present** - This is an exercise prompt slide with no mathematical equations displayed\n\n### 3) GRAPH DETAILS\n**No graphs shown** - This slide contains exercise instructions that will require students to create loanable funds market diagrams showing:\n- Initial equilibrium with balanced budget\n- New equilibrium after budget deficit\n- Equilibrium changes under budget surplus scenarios\n\n### 4) KEY DEFINITIONS OR EMPHASIZED TEXT\n\n**Scenario Setup:**\n- Government begins with a **balanced budget**\n- Budget deficit occurs due to:\n  - **Increase in government spending** and/or\n  - **Decrease in taxes**\n\n**Exercise Components (emphasized in red):**\n\n**Part A:** \n- Draw equilibrium change diagram\n- Analyze effects on **equilibrium interest rate**\n- Analyze effects on **equilibrium investment**\n\n**Part B:**\n- **Analyze the effects of a budget surplus**\n\n**Analytical Framework:**\n- Use **loanable funds model** for analysis\n- Focus on equilibrium changes and market adjustments",
      "text": "Active Learning 2: Budget deficits and surpluses\nAssume the government starts with a balanced budget and then,\nbecause of an increase in government spending (and/or decrease in\ntaxes), starts running a budget deficit. Use the loanable funds model to\nanalyze the effects of a government budget deficit"
    },
