      "vision_extract": "## Slide Analysis: Angel's Marginal Cost Curve\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\nAngel's Marginal Cost Curve - illustrating the relationship between quantity of output and marginal cost, demonstrating the typical U-shaped marginal cost curve in producer theory.\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\nNo explicit equations are shown on this slide.\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**Axes:**\n- X-axis: Quantity of output (Q), ranging from 0 to 10\n- Y-axis: Costs, ranging from $1 to $35\n\n**Curve:**\n- Red U-shaped marginal cost (MC) curve with red dots marking data points\n- Curve labeled \"MC\"\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Curve starts at approximately $15 (Q=1)\n- Reaches minimum at approximately Q=4, MC=$2\n- Rises steeply after the minimum point\n- Ends at approximately $32 (Q=10)\n\n**Intersections:**\nNo specific intersections with other curves are shown.\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n**Data Table showing:**\n- **Q (Quantity):** 0 through 10 units\n- **TC (Total Cost):** Starting at $18 (fixed cost) and increasing to $154\n- **MC (Marginal Cost):** Values ranging from $15.0 down to $2.0 (minimum) then increasing to $32.0\n\n**Key pattern:** The marginal cost decreases initially (from $15.0 to $2.0), reaches a minimum at Q=4, then increases substantially, demonstrating the typical U-shaped marginal cost curve characteristic of short-run production with diminishing marginal returns.",
      "text": "Angel\u2019s Marginal Cost Curve\nQ TC MC\n0 $18\nCosts\n$15.0\n35\n$\n1 33\n10.0\n30 MC\n2 43\n5.0\n3 48 25\n2.0\n4 50 20\n4.0\n5 54 15\n8.0\n6 62\n10\n14.0\n7 76\n5\n20.0\n8 96\n0\n26.0\n9 122\n0 5 10 Q\n32.0\n10 154 Quantity of output\nMankiw, Principles of Economics, 10th Edition. \u00a9 2024 Cengage. All Rights Reserved. May not be sc"
    },
