      "image": "slide_graphs/WEEK_5_PRODUCER_THEORY_s064.png",
      "vision_extract": "## Slide 64 Analysis - Producer Theory: Cost Calculations\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\n**Active Learning Exercise: Calculating production costs** - Students must complete missing values in a cost analysis table showing the relationship between different cost measures across varying output levels.\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\nNo explicit equations are displayed, but the table implies standard cost relationships:\n- TC = VC + FC (where FC = $50)\n- AFC = FC \u00f7 Q\n- AVC = VC \u00f7 Q  \n- ATC = TC \u00f7 Q (or AFC + AVC)\n- MC = Change in TC \u00f7 Change in Q\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**Table Structure:**\n- **Columns:** Q (Quantity), VC (Variable Cost), TC (Total Cost), AFC (Average Fixed Cost), AVC (Average Variable Cost), ATC (Average Total Cost), MC (Marginal Cost)\n- **Rows:** Output levels from 0 to 6 units\n- **Given values:** Scattered across table requiring calculation of missing entries\n- **Key data points:** FC = $50 (derived from Q=0, TC=$50), various cost values provided as anchors\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n- **\"Active Learning\"** (highlighted in red) - emphasizes interactive exercise format\n- **\"Fill in the blank spaces of this table\"** - clear instruction for student activity\n- **Cost abbreviations used:**\n  - Q = Quantity of output\n  - VC = Variable Cost\n  - TC = Total Cost  \n  - AFC = Average Fixed Cost\n  - AVC = Average Variable Cost\n  - ATC = Average Total Cost\n  - MC = Marginal Cost\n- **\"n/a\"** entries for Q=0 where average costs are undefined",
      "text": "Active Learning: Calculating costs\nFill in the blank spaces of this table.\nQ VC TC AFC AVC ATC MC\n0 $50 n/a n/a n/a\n$10\n1 10 $10 $60.00\n2 30 80\n30\n3 16.67 20 36.67\n4 100 150 12.50 37.50\n5 150 30\n60\n6 210 260 8.33 35 43.33\nMankiw, Principles of Economics, 10th Edition. \u00a9 2024 Cengage. All Rights Rese"
    },
