      "image": "slide_graphs/WEEK_5_PRODUCER_THEORY_s079.png",
      "vision_extract": "## SLIDE 79 ANALYSIS\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\n**Marginal Cost (MC) and the Firm's Supply Decision** - specifically demonstrating how the MC curve functions as the firm's supply curve by showing the relationship between price changes and optimal quantity decisions.\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\nNo explicit equations are displayed on this slide.\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**Axes:**\n- X-axis: Q (Quantity)\n- Y-axis: Costs\n\n**Curves:**\n- MC curve: Upward-sloping blue line labeled \"MC\"\n- Two horizontal lines representing marginal revenue at different price levels\n\n**Labels:**\n- P\u2081, P\u2082 (price levels, where P\u2082 > P\u2081)\n- Q\u2081, Q\u2082 (corresponding quantities, where Q\u2082 > Q\u2081)\n- MR\u2081, MR\u2082 (marginal revenue lines)\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Two intersection points marked with black dots where MC intersects with MR\u2081 and MR\u2082\n- Corresponding equilibrium points at (Q\u2081, P\u2081) and (Q\u2082, P\u2082)\n\n**Intersections:**\n- MC = MR\u2081 at quantity Q\u2081\n- MC = MR\u2082 at quantity Q\u2082\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n- **\"the MC curve is the firm's supply curve\"** (emphasized in blue text box)\n- **\"If price rises to P\u2082, then the profit-maximizing quantity rises to Q\u2082\"**\n- **\"The MC curve determines the firm's Q at any price\"**\n- **\"Hence, the MC curve is the firm's supply curve\"** (conclusion statement in blue)",
      "text": "MC and the Firm\u2019s Supply Decision \u2013 2\nIf price rises to P , the MC curve is\n2\nthe firm\u2019s supply\nthen the profit-\nCosts\ncurve.\nmaximizing quantity\nMC\nrises to Q .\n2\nP MR\n2 2\nThe MC curve\ndetermines the\nfirm\u2019s Q at any price. P MR\n1 1\nHence, the MC curve\nis the firm\u2019s supply\nQ\ncurve.\nQ Q\n1 2\nMankiw, P"
