      "image": "slide_graphs/WEEK_5_PRODUCER_THEORY_s095.png",
      "vision_extract": "## Slide Analysis: Amari's Profit Example\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\n- **Profit maximization graphical analysis** using Amari's business example\n- Demonstration of optimal quantity determination where MR = MC\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\n- **Basic profit equation**: Profit = TR - TC\n- **Per-unit profit equation**: Profit = (P - ATC) \u00d7 Q\n- **Numerical calculation**: = (20 - 15) \u00d7 7 = 140 - 105 = $35\n- **Total Revenue**: TR = P \u00d7 Q = $140\n- **Total Cost**: TC = ATC \u00d7 Q = $105\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**Axes:**\n- Vertical axis: Costs, P (price/cost in dollars)\n- Horizontal axis: Q (quantity in bushels of apples)\n\n**Curves and Lines:**\n- **MC curve**: Upward-sloping blue marginal cost curve\n- **ATC curve**: U-shaped blue average total cost curve\n- **MR\u2081 line**: Horizontal red line at P\u2081 = $20 (marginal revenue)\n\n**Key Points and Values:**\n- **Optimal quantity**: Q\u2081 = 7 bushels (where MR = MC)\n- **Price**: P\u2081 = $20\n- **Average Total Cost**: ATC\u2081 = $15\n- **Intersection point**: MR\u2081 and MC curves intersect at optimal output level\n\n**Shaded Areas:**\n- **Profit rectangle**: Shaded area between price line ($20) and ATC line ($15) from Q = 0 to Q = 7\n\n### 4) Key Definitions/Emphasized Text\n- **Profit maximization rule**: \"Find Q where MR = MC\" (highlighted in purple text)\n- **Unit of measurement**: Bushels of apples\n- **Profit calculation method**: Demonstrated both as total (TR - TC) and per-unit [(P - ATC) \u00d7 Q] approaches",
      "text": "EXAMPLE: Amari\u2019s Profit: the graph\nProfit = TR \u2013 TC\nMC\nCosts, P Find Q\nwhere MR =\nProfit = (P \u2013 ATC) \u00d7 Q\nMC\n= (20 \u2013 15) * 7 P = $20 MR\n1 1\nATC\n= 140 \u2013 105 = $35\nATC = $15\n1\nTR = P \u00d7 Q = $140\nTC = ATC \u00d7 Q = $105\nQ = 7 Q\n1\n(bushels of apples)\nMankiw, Principles of Economics, 10th Edition. \u00a9 2024 Cenga"
    },
