      "vision_extract": "## Slide 176 Analysis: Demand Curves: Competitive Firm vs. Monopoly\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\nComparison of demand curves faced by competitive firms versus monopolistic firms, focusing on the relationship between price (P) and marginal revenue (MR) in each market structure.\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\n- **P = MR** (for competitive firm)\n- **MR \u2260 P** (for monopolist, shown in red text for emphasis)\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n\n**Left Graph - Competitive Firm:**\n- **Axes:** P (price) on vertical axis, Q (quantity) on horizontal axis\n- **Curve:** Horizontal line labeled \"D\" \n- **Key characteristic:** Perfectly elastic demand curve\n- **Label:** \"A competitive firm's demand curve\"\n\n**Right Graph - Monopolist:**\n- **Axes:** P (price) on vertical axis, Q (quantity) on horizontal axis  \n- **Curve:** Downward-sloping line labeled \"D\"\n- **Key characteristic:** Negatively sloped demand curve\n- **Label:** \"A monopolist's demand curve\" and \"The market demand curve\"\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n\n**For Competitive Firm:**\n- \"The firm can increase Q without lowering P, so MR = P for the competitive firm.\"\n\n**For Monopolist:**\n- \"To sell a larger Q, the firm must reduce P. Thus, MR \u2260 P.\" (MR \u2260 P is emphasized in red)\n\n**Market Structure Distinction:**\n- Competitive firms face perfectly elastic demand (horizontal)\n- Monopolists face the entire market demand curve (downward-sloping)",
      "text": "Demand Curves: Competitive Firm vs. Monopoly\nA competitive A monopolist\u2019s\nP P\nfirm\u2019s demand demand curve\ncurve\nP = MR\nD\nThe market\ndemand curve\nD\nQ Q\nThe firm can increase To sell a larger Q, the\nQ without lowering P, firm must reduce P.\nso MR = P for the Thus, MR \u2260 P.\ncompetitive firm.\nMankiw, Prin"
