      "vision_extract": "## SLIDE 177 ANALYSIS\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\n**Revenue Analysis for Monopolistic Market** - Active learning exercise analyzing total revenue (TR), average revenue (AR), and marginal revenue (MR) for \"JJ's Hairdo,\" the only hair salon in town (monopoly market structure).\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\nNo explicit equations are displayed on this slide. The exercise focuses on calculating revenue metrics from the given demand schedule.\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**No graph present.** The slide contains a data table with the following structure:\n- **Table format:** 5 columns \u00d7 11 rows\n- **Column headers:** Q, P, TR, AR, MR\n- **Complete data provided for:**\n  - Q (Quantity): 0-10 units\n  - P (Price): $60 (at Q=0) decreasing by $5 increments to $10 (at Q=10)\n- **Incomplete columns:** TR, AR, and MR columns are blank (to be filled by students)\n- **Visual elements:** Diagonal striping in MR column cells for Q=0 and Q=10\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n- **Market context:** \"Jayla and Jaden own the only hair salon in town, 'JJ's hairdo'\" - establishes monopoly market structure\n- **Data source:** \"The table shows the market demand for haircuts\"\n- **Learning objectives (emphasized in blue text):**\n  - \"Fill in the missing spaces of the table\"\n  - \"What is the relation between P and AR?\"\n  - \"Between P and MR?\"\n\n**Key variables:**\n- **Q:** Quantity of haircuts\n- **P:** Price per haircut\n- **TR:** Total Revenue\n- **AR:** Average Revenue  \n- **MR:** Marginal Revenue",
