      "vision_extract": "## Slide 48 Analysis: Monopoly Profit Maximization\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\nMonopoly Profit Maximization - explaining how monopolists determine optimal quantity and pricing strategy\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\n- **MR = MC** (profit-maximizing condition)\n- **P > MR = MC** (pricing relationship for monopoly)\n- **P > ATC** (profit condition)\n\n### 3) Graph Details\nNo graphs present on this slide\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n\n**Primary Rule:**\n- Produce Q where **MR = MC** (emphasized in red)\n\n**Pricing Strategy:**\n- Sets the highest price consumers are willing to pay for that quantity\n- Finds this price on the **D curve** (demand curve, emphasized in blue)\n\n**Key Relationships:**\n- **P > MR = MC** - Price exceeds marginal revenue at profit-maximizing point\n- **If P > ATC** - Condition under which the monopoly earns a profit\n\n**Variable Definitions:**\n- Q = Quantity\n- MR = Marginal Revenue  \n- MC = Marginal Cost\n- P = Price\n- ATC = Average Total Cost\n- D = Demand curve",
