      "vision_extract": "## Slide 49 Analysis: Profit-Maximization for a Monopoly\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\nProfit-maximization for a monopoly firm and the determination of optimal output and pricing\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\n**MR = MC** (profit-maximizing condition, emphasized in red text)\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**Axes:**\n- X-axis: Quantity\n- Y-axis: Costs and Revenue\n\n**Curves:**\n- **MC (Marginal Cost)**: Red upward-sloping curve\n- **MR (Marginal Revenue)**: Red downward-sloping curve\n- **D (Demand)**: Blue downward-sloping curve, positioned above MR curve\n\n**Key Points and Intersections:**\n- Intersection of MR and MC curves determines optimal quantity Q\n- From quantity Q, a vertical dashed line extends upward\n- From quantity Q, the price P is found where the vertical line intersects the demand curve D\n- Horizontal dashed line from price P extends to the y-axis\n\n**Labels:**\n- Q marked on x-axis at profit-maximizing quantity\n- P marked on y-axis at profit-maximizing price\n- Black dot shows the intersection point of MR and MC\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n- **\"The profit-maximizing Q is where MR = MC\"** (main profit-maximization rule)\n- **\"At this Q, find P on the demand curve\"** (pricing instruction)\n- **\"Profit-maximizing output\"** (label for the optimal quantity Q)",
