      "image": "slide_graphs/WEEK_6_PRODUCER_THEORY_II_s106.png",
      "vision_extract": "## Slide Analysis: Economics Lecture Slide 106\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\n**Market Structure Comparisons** - Comparative analysis of three major market structures: Perfect Competition, Monopolistic Competition, and Monopoly\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\nNone present\n\n### 3) Graph Details\nNo graphs present - this is a comparative table format\n\n### 4) Key Definitions and Emphasized Content\n\n**Comparative Table Structure:**\n- **Columns:** Perfect Competition | Monopolistic Competition | Monopoly\n- **Row Categories:**\n\n**Number of sellers:**\n- Perfect Competition: Many\n- Monopolistic Competition: Many  \n- Monopoly: One\n\n**Free entry/exit:**\n- Perfect Competition: Yes\n- Monopolistic Competition: Yes\n- Monopoly: No\n\n**Long-run economic profits:**\n- Perfect Competition: Zero\n- Monopolistic Competition: Zero\n- Monopoly: Positive\n\n**The products firms sell:**\n- Perfect Competition: Identical\n- Monopolistic Competition: Differentiated\n- Monopoly: No close substitutes\n\n**Firm has market power?**\n- Perfect Competition: None; price-taker\n- Monopolistic Competition: Yes\n- Monopoly: Yes\n\n**D curve facing firm:**\n- Perfect Competition: Horizontal\n- Monopolistic Competition: Downward-sloping\n- Monopoly: Downward-sloping (market D)\n\n**Key Emphasized Terms:**\n- Price-taker (Perfect Competition)\n- Product differentiation (Monopolistic Competition)\n- Market power\n- Demand curve characteristics for each structure",
      "text": "Comparisons\nPerfect Monopolistic\nCompetition Competition Monopoly\nNumber of sellers Many Many One\nFree entry/exit Yes Yes No\nLong-run\neconomic profits Zero Zero Positive\nThe products No close\nfirms sell Identical Differentiated substitutes\nFirm has market None;\npower? price-taker Yes Yes\nD curve Dow"
