      "image": "slide_graphs/WEEK_6_PRODUCER_THEORY_II_s108.png",
      "vision_extract": "## Slide 108 Analysis: Short Run Equilibrium\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic:\nShort-run equilibrium and profit maximization for monopolistically competitive firms\n\n### 2) Equations Shown:\n- **MR = MC** (profit maximization condition)\n- **P > ATC** (profit condition)\n- **P < ATC** (loss condition)\n\n### 3) Graph Details:\nNo graph present on this slide\n\n### 4) Key Definitions and Emphasized Text:\n\n**Main Framework:**\n- **Profit maximization in the short-run for the monopolistically competitive firm**\n\n**Decision Rules:**\n- **Quantity Decision:** Produce the quantity where MR = MC\n- **Price Decision:** Price is determined on the demand curve\n- **Profit/Loss Conditions:**\n  - If P > ATC: firm earns profit\n  - If P < ATC: firm incurs loss\n\n**Market Structure Comparison:**\n- Behavior is \"similar to monopoly\" in terms of profit maximization approach\n\n**Key Terms:**\n- MR (Marginal Revenue)\n- MC (Marginal Cost) \n- ATC (Average Total Cost)\n- P (Price)\n\nThis slide establishes the fundamental short-run decision-making framework for monopolistically competitive firms, emphasizing the monopoly-like profit maximization rule while introducing the profit/loss determination based on price-cost relationships.",
      "text": "Short Run Equilibrium\n\u2022 Profit maximization in the short-run for the\nmonopolistically competitive firm:\n\u2013 Produce the quantity where MR = MC\n\u2013 Price: on the demand curve\n\u2013 If P > ATC: profit\n\u2013 If P < ATC: loss\n\u2013 Similar to monopoly\n\u00a9 2018 Cengage Learning\u00ae. May not be scanned, copied or duplicated, "
    },
