      "image": "slide_graphs/WEEK_6_PRODUCER_THEORY_II_s109.png",
      "vision_extract": "## Slide 109 Analysis: Monopolistically Competitive Firm Earning Profits in the Short Run\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\nMonopolistically competitive firm earning profits in the short run and its profit maximization behavior\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\n- **MR < P** (at each Q)\n- **MR = MC** (profit maximization condition)\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**Axes:**\n- X-axis: Quantity (Q)\n- Y-axis: Price\n\n**Curves:**\n- **D curve**: Blue, downward-sloping demand curve (labeled \"D\")\n- **MR curve**: Red, downward-sloping marginal revenue curve (labeled \"MR\")\n- **MC curve**: Red, U-shaped marginal cost curve (labeled \"MC\")\n- **ATC curve**: Blue, U-shaped average total cost curve (labeled \"ATC\")\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Intersection of MR and MC curves determines optimal quantity Q\n- Price P is determined from the demand curve at quantity Q\n- ATC level shown at quantity Q\n\n**Intersections:**\n- MR = MC intersection (profit maximization point)\n\n**Shaded Area:**\n- Orange/tan rectangular area representing profit (between price P and ATC, extending to quantity Q)\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n- **\"The firm faces a downward-sloping D curve\"**\n- **\"At each Q, MR < P\"** (emphasized in red)\n- **\"To maximize profit, firm produces Q where MR = MC\"** (MR = MC in red)\n- **\"The firm uses the D curve to set P\"** (D curve emphasized in red)\n- **\"profit\"** (labeled on shaded area)",
      "text": "A Monopolistically Competitive Firm Earning\nProfits in the Short Run\nThe firm faces a Price\nMC\nprofit\ndownward-sloping\nD curve. ATC\nP\nAt each Q, MR < P.\nATC\nD\nTo maximize profit,\nfirm produces Q\nMR\nwhere MR = MC.\nQ\nQuantity\nThe firm uses the\nD curve to set P.\n\u00a9 2018 Cengage Learning\u00ae. May not be sca"
