      "vision_extract": "## Slide Analysis: Economics Lecture Slide 125\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\n**Interpreting the payoff matrix** - Introduction to game theory and payoff matrix analysis in producer theory\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\nNo mathematical equations are present on this slide.\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n**Payoff Matrix Structure:**\n- **Format:** 2\u00d72 matrix table\n- **Players:** Anil (row player) vs. Bala (column player)\n- **Strategies:**\n  - Anil's strategies: Rice, Cassava\n  - Bala's strategies: Rice, Cassava\n- **Payoff Values:**\n  - (Rice, Rice): 3, 1\n  - (Rice, Cassava): 2, 2\n  - (Cassava, Rice): 4, 4\n  - (Cassava, Cassava): 1, 3\n- **Visual Elements:** \n  - Purple header for Bala\n  - Blue side label for Anil\n  - Light purple/gray cells containing payoff pairs\n  - Each cell contains two numbers representing payoffs for each player\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n**Payoff matrix** = A table of the payoffs associated with every possible combination of strategies chosen by two or more players in a game\n\n**Additional Elements:**\n- Course identifier: \"CORE ESPP\" (bottom right corner)\n- Context: Part of Week 6 Producer Theory II curriculum",
      "text": "Interpreting the payoff matrix\nPayoff matrix = A table of the payoffs associated with every possible\ncombination of strategies chosen by two or more players in a game"
