      "image": "slide_graphs/WEEK_8_THEORY_OF_CONSUMER_CHOICE_s067.png",
      "vision_extract": "## Slide 67 Analysis: Less Extreme Cases\n\n### 1) Main Concept/Topic\n**Less Extreme Cases of Substitutes and Complements** - Examining indifference curves for goods that are close substitutes and close complements, which represent more realistic scenarios compared to perfect substitutes/complements.\n\n### 2) Equations Shown\nNo equations are displayed on this slide.\n\n### 3) Graph Details\n\n**Left Graph:**\n- **Axes:** \n  - X-axis: Quantity of Coke\n  - Y-axis: Quantity of Pepsi\n- **Curve:** Green indifference curve\n- **Shape:** Downward sloping, slightly bowed (concave to origin)\n- **Key characteristics:** Moderate curvature indicating some substitutability but not perfect\n\n**Right Graph:**\n- **Axes:**\n  - X-axis: Quantity of hot dogs\n  - Y-axis: Quantity of hot dog buns\n- **Curve:** Orange/brown indifference curve\n- **Shape:** Downward sloping, very bowed (highly concave to origin)\n- **Key characteristics:** Sharp curvature indicating strong complementarity\n\n### 4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text\n\n**Close Substitutes (highlighted in green box):**\n- \"Indifference curves for close substitutes are not very bowed\"\n\n**Close Complements (highlighted in orange box):**\n- \"Indifference curves for close complements are very bowed\"\n\n**Examples provided:**\n- Close substitutes: Pepsi and Coke\n- Close complements: Hot dogs and hot dog buns\n\nThe slide demonstrates how the degree of curvature in indifference curves reflects the relationship between goods - less bowed curves indicate greater substitutability, while more bowed curves indicate greater complementarity.",
      "text": "Less Extreme Cases:\nClose Substitutes and Close Complements\nIndifference Indifference\nQuantity\nQuantity\ncurves for close of hot curves for\nof Pepsi\ndog buns\nsubstitutes are close\nnot very bowed complements\nare very\nbowed\nQuantity Quantity\nof Coke of hot dogs\n\u00a9 2018 Cengage Learning\u00ae. May not be scan"
