      "vision_extract": "## Slide 129 Analysis\n\n**1) Main Concept/Topic:**\nJob Search and Frictional Unemployment\n\n**2) Equations Shown:**\nNone\n\n**3) Graph Details:**\nNo graphs present\n\n**4) Key Definitions or Emphasized Text:**\n\n**Primary Definitions:**\n- **Job search**: Process by which workers find appropriate jobs given their tastes and skills\n\n**Key Emphasized Concepts:**\n- **\"Some frictional unemployment is inevitable\"** (emphasized in red text)\n\n**Supporting Explanations:**\n- **Sectoral shifts** (underlined): changes in the composition of demand among industries or regions\n- Two main causes of inevitable frictional unemployment:\n  - Because the economy is always changing\n  - Changing patterns of international trade\n\n**Structure:**\nThe slide presents job search as a fundamental labor market process, establishing that frictional unemployment cannot be eliminated due to constant economic changes, specifically sectoral shifts and evolving international trade patterns.",
